WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.650
While some movies are universally acclaimed,
and others we can all pretty much agree are

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.440
just garbage.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:11.060
But then there's a third category: films that
inspire both adoration AND disgust, blockbusters

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.180
that split audiences completely in half.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.940
This phenomenon spans all genres, but these
films all have one thing in common—they're

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.860
movies everyone either loves or hates.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.400
Forrest Gump

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:28.600
When Forrest Gump hit theaters in 1994, it
grossed $677 million worldwide and won six

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.540
Academy Awards.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:34.480
It elevated Tom Hanks from actor to superstar,
and many of its iconic lines are still quoted

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:34.980
today.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.900
"Run, forrest.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.220
Run!"

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.760
It's currently ranked on IMDB as the 12th
best film of all time, and has a 95% audience

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.520
approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.220
But for all the love Gump has received, it's
picked up some haters, too.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.060
"He must be the stupidest son of a bitch alive,
but he sure is fast!"

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:02.600
It caused a huge upset when it beat Pulp Fiction
for best picture at the Academy Awards.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.659
Many right-wing news outlets have lauded Forrest
Gump as one of the best conservative films

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.380
of all time.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.811
But to put it simply, critics feel the movie
is all melodrama with no real message, while

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.000
fans love it for its simple perspective of
a complicated world.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:18.780
"life was like a box of chocolates.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.860
You never know what you're gonna get."

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:24.700
Titanic

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:30.520
Sailing into theaters in 1997, Titanic became
the highest-grossing film of all time.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.280
The epic period piece became a major cultural
touchstone, inspiring everyone who's ever

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.420
been on a boat to shout the iconic line:

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.800
"I'm the king of the world!"

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.940
"I'm king of the world!"

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.800
"Hey, somebody has to do this: I'm king of
the WWWWWWW"

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.840
"Don't ruin a perfect week!"

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:56.819
Its beautiful costumes, tragic romance and
revolutionary special effects touched so many

00:01:56.819 --> 00:02:01.009
moviegoers that Roger Ebert wrote an entire
essay about how he could "hear the warmth

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:04.480
in people's voices when they discuss it and
see the light in their eyes."

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:08.340
But critic Owen Gleiberman says the film "gave
rise to hater culture."

00:02:08.349 --> 00:02:12.300
For every enthusiast, there's a cynic who
feels the film is too cliché, and that its

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.620
theme song, My Heart Will Go On, should only
be played for prisoners.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.720
Even Kate Winslet herself said the song made
her want to throw up.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.720
"How often do you listen to Celine Dion's
My Heart Will Go On?"

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.880
"absolutely never."

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.200
People have also not been able to let go of
the fact that Jack absolutely could have fit

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.890
on the door with Rose instead of freezing
to death in the ocean.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.280
he should have tried harder to get on that
door.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.000
I think he could have

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:35.500
"totally enough room, right?"

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.080
"YES!!!"

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:41.640
But for the most part, fans think the film
is romantic perfection, while the haters just

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.780
think it's romantic fluff.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.290
At least everyone can agree on the romance
angle, though!

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.300
"You know, No matter how noble Jack's intentions
might have been, sometimes discretion is the

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.500
better part of valor."

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.010
The Passion of the Christ

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.260
Deadpool may the highest-grossing R-rated
film worldwide, but when it comes to the domestic

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.160
box office, The Passion of the Christ is the
king of kings.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.800
The biblical gorefest earned $370 million
at home, which is largely thanks to Christian

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:08.300
moviegoers.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.920
Some congregations rented out theaters for
special screenings, while others actually

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.540
screened the film in their churches.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:17.460
"The faithful are flocking to this theatre
this morning.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.320
The Passion is playing on all 20 screens."

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.020
One man was so passionate that he bought 6,000
tickets and gave them away for free.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.700
But many people saw the movie as anti-Semitic
for its murder-hungry mobster portrayal of

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:34.190
Jews, along with the fact that director Mel
Gibson refused to have any Jewish scholars

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.780
advise him on the subject matter.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.700
Audiences were also shocked by the film's
extreme violence.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.480
"It was very graphic.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.720
Yeah, extremely graphic.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.300
But it was probably true to life."

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:48.340
Considering the subject material, it's no
wonder audiences either hailed Gibson as a

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:51.480
cinematic saint or crucified him for his controversial
film.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.600
No Country for Old Men

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:59.120
In 2007, the world was introduced to Anton
Chigurh, one of the most iconic bad guys in

00:03:59.120 --> 00:03:59.820
movie history.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.620
"what's the most you ever lost on a coin toss?"

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.820
"the most you ever lost on a coin toss?"

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:13.400
No Country for Old Men won four Academy Awards,
including best picture, and was hailed as

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.290
one of the Coen brothers' best movies.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.880
It is currently ranked by IMDB as the 159th
best film of all time.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.340
But a lot of people couldn't get past the
movie's ending.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.340
The hero dies, the bad guy gets away, and
after Tommy Lee Jones chats about his mysterious

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.680
dream, the movie cuts to black.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.780
For those who were expecting a conventional
finale, it's one of the most infuriating movie

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:35.860
endings of all-time.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.980
Leading man Josh Brolin knew the ending was
going to tick people off, and told MTV:

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.590
"I love that people leave the movie saying,
'I hate the ending.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.500
I was so pissed.'

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.620
Good, it was supposed to piss you off."

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:47.620
The Dark Knight Rises

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:52.220
The Dark Knight Rises was surrounded by so
much hype that fanboys and Christopher Nolan

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.900
himself were defending it before it even hit
theaters in 2012.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:00.200
When film critic Marshall Fine posted the
first negative review, his website crashed

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.080
under the rush of angry responses.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:06.100
Rotten Tomatoes eventually had to shut down
the film's comments section, a first in the

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.080
website's history.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:11.280
Despite a spirited defense from hardcore fans,
the film has been picked apart for plot holes

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.940
and logical inconsistencies.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.740
Moviegoers were also upset with the film's
ending, which showed Bruce Wayne alive and

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.020
well and on vacation with Selina Kyle.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.850
Some thought the movie was a critique of the
Occupy Wall Street movement, while others

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:26.980
suspected that Bane was a metaphor for republican
presidential hopeful Mitt Romney.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.360
"Calm down Dr., now is not that time for fear.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.140
That comes later."

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:37.740
Inspiring everything from death threats to
devastating takedowns, The Dark Knight Rises

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.440
is Nolan's most hotly contested movie to date.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.220
Man of Steel

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:47.400
Depending on who you ask, Man of Steel is
either the best Superman movie or the worst.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:52.270
Zack Snyder's depiction of Superman as a cynical,
complex and tortured hero stood out in stark

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.720
contrast to the colorful and quippy films
Marvel had been cranking out.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:00.960
Many fans appreciated this somber take, and
the film earned $668 million worldwide.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:05.400
However, many fans preferred Christopher Reeve's
cheerful and fun version of Superman to this

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.940
dark and gritty approach.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:11.260
Others were horrified by the sheer volume
of collateral damage amassed during Superman's

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.520
duel with General Zod.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.980
But perhaps the biggest controversy came when
the man of steel straight-up murders his enemy,

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.960
a move that seemed to go against Clark Kent's
strict moral code.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:24.160
Even producer Christopher Nolan initially
opposed the ending, which producer David S.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.760
Goyer revealed on The Empire Film Podcast.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:31.160
"killing zod was a big thing and something
that Chris Nolan originally said there's

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.180
no way you can do this."

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:36.460
The murder made it into the film, and sent
the man of steel in a direction that not everyone

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:37.160
was happy with.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.000
La La Land

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:43.460
When La La Land danced into theaters, it won
over audiences and critics alike.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:48.060
It's also tied with Titanic and All About
Eve for earning the most Oscar nominations

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.740
ever -- 14 in total.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:54.720
Audiences far and wide were touched by this
movie-musical homage and love letter to Hollywood,

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.960
which was written and directed by Damien Chazelle.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.720
However, for every La La Land fan, there's
a cynic rolling their eyes.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:05.340
Many were annoyed by Ryan Gosling's Sebastian,
who was portrayed as the white savior of jazz,

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.960
a genre that was pioneered by black musicians.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:11.420
"it's dying, Mia, it's dying on the vine.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:12.860
And the world says 'let it die.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.540
It had it's time.'

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:16.220
Well, not on my watch."

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:21.160
Others felt Emma Stone's character, Mia, was
far less complex than her male counterpart.

00:07:21.169 --> 00:07:25.590
Ultimately, La La Land was a movie made for
the ones who dream, but for many people, that

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.400
dream was a nightmare.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:27.780
mother!

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:32.880
When it comes to polarizing his audience,
director Darren Aronofsky has outdone himself

00:07:32.889 --> 00:07:36.960
with mother!, an allegorical horror film that
traps Jennifer Lawrence in a never-ending

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.660
nightmare of strangers with no respect for
personal space.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:45.100
The film was not for everyone, scoring a middling
69% on the tomatometer and an audience score

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.060
of 50%.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.991
While horror fans enjoyed how gruesome and
bloody it was, others argued that the film

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.520
was too heavy-handed with its allegories and
symbolism.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.700
"you never loved me.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.480
You just loved how much I loved you."

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.260
"I gave you everything!"

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:06.860
Needless to say, with the way mother! divided
its audience, it might be the very epitome

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.360
of a "love it or hate it" film.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:10.200
The Last Jedi

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:14.910
When Rey tracked down Luke Skywalker in The
Force Awakens, fans around the world couldn't

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:17.320
wait to see what would happen in the next
Star Wars film.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:20.760
Two years later, The Last Jedi caused a great
disturbance in the force.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:25.220
Directed by Rian Johnson, it quickly became
one of the best-reviewed films of the franchise,

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:29.380
with some critics hailing it as the best Star
Wars film since The Empire Strikes Back.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:34.680
Fans praised the film for subverting expectations,
demystifying the Jedi mythology, and paving

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.200
a new path for the franchise.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:41.110
However, many Star Wars fans saw The Last
Jedi as an attack on George Lucas's original

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:41.620
universe.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:46.820
While the film scored a 91% approval rating
on Rotten Tomatoes, its audience score currently

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.560
sits at only 47%.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:52.560
The biggest upset seemed to have to do with
Luke Skywalker, whose portrayal as a moody

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:55.130
pessimist upset even Mark Hamill, who played
him.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:01.700
"I think the world of Rian Johnson, I said to
him I fundamentally disagree with what you

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:02.700
think about Luke."

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.420
Then again, audiences weren't too pleased
with The Empire Strikes Back when it was first

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.420
released either.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:10.900
Maybe in a few decades, fans will look back
on The Last Jedi with a little more fondness,

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:11.400
too.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:12.580
Bright

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:17.820
Described on Deadline as "Lethal Weapon meets
Lord of the Rings," Bright unfortunately did

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.720
not live up to any of the hype surrounding
it.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:24.360
The Netflix original movie, which was written
by Max Landis and directed by David Ayer,

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.840
was universally hailed as a total mess.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:31.620
From its sloppy world-building to cringe-worthy
dialogue, not even Will Smith's charisma could

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:36.040
save Bright from scoring an abysmal 26% approval
rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:38.800
"fairy lives DON'T matter today."

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:43.700
Somehow, though, its audience approval rating
on Rotten Tomatoes currently sits at 85%.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:47.920
Netflix president Reed Hasting said Bright
was one of the site's "most viewed original

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:50.730
titles ever," and a sequel is already in the
works.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:54.540
For whatever reason, plenty of people watched
Bright, which seems to be the only aspect

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:56.160
of the film that anyone can agree on.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:57.820
Thanks for watching!

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.260
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:02.410
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

